Description: screenShield: reuse the unlock dialog and fix remaining leaks
 Every lock/unlock cycle allocates a brand new UnlockDialog (password entry,
 clock, notifications box, background actors, GPU-backed Cogl textures) and
 destroys the old one. GJS/SpiderMonkey does not run garbage collection
 between cycles, so the destroyed Clutter actor tree's memory accumulates as
 anonymous heap (Private_Dirty) rather than being reclaimed promptly -
 roughly 4-10 MB per lock/unlock cycle, growing linearly with usage.
 .
 This keeps a single UnlockDialog instance alive for the life of the
 ScreenShield and just hides/re-shows it instead of destroy()/recreate.
 .
 Additionally:
 - _lockScreenShown's GLib.timeout_add_once is now tracked and cancelled.
 - _hidePointerUntilMotion guards against duplicate signal handlers.
 - System.gc() is called after deactivation to reclaim Clutter transitions.
